This file contains upgrading tools/scripts/...

Usually you should stop whole BBS and then run scripts here.

With nest.svc (CONFIG_NEST), the files of the boards (.DIR, articles)
are only its cache, and .BRD is mirrored into it. These tools write the
files directly, not through BoF, so:

 - Run the tools that rewrite posts or .DIR (convert_utf8, convert_sgr_66,
   fix_2026h, dir_recommend_to_rating) before the boards are imported into
   nest.svc (`nest.ctl import-board`); on a site already on nest.svc, the
   next render or sync of nest.svc reverts them. Stop nest.svc, run them,
   and import the boards again.
 - After the tools that rewrite .BRD (board_split_title,
   migrate_board_moderators), run `nest.ctl import-boards`.

comment_readonly keeps the comments of the boards with moderators as they
are (BRD_COMMENT_READONLY: people may neither edit nor delete their own),
as many moderators want when the comments move to nest.svc. Run it by hand
once when switching (dry run unless -w); it writes .BRD through BoF, which
tells nest.svc.

clean_log_posts moves the logs that were posted to Security (by the old
bin/account: usies, up to ~350 MB a day, the song log and the money log;
by openticket: the bets of each lottery; by mailog.sh: a part of mailog)
into adm/YYYY/<name>/<name>-YYYYMMDD.zst (.gz without zstd), where
bin/rotatelog now keeps them, checking each archive. It also removes the
posts that only copied others or that nobody needs, no longer made: the
results of lotteries in Security and Record, and in Record the starts of
lotteries, the results of polls (all on their boards), the chicken report
and the empty lists of spam mails. Fewer posts make the import into
nest.svc faster. It recompresses the old adm/usies-YYMMDD.gz and
adm/mailog-YYMMDD.gz into adm/YYYY/ too. It writes .DIR directly: run it
once, by hand, after installing bin/rotatelog and before the boards are
imported into nest.svc (dry run unless -w; -n N to try it on N posts of
each board first; zstd -9 takes a few seconds for a 350 MB day, -l 19
makes it 20% smaller in ~1.5 minutes).

See docs/nest_migration.md.
